<!-- QUARRY:PART:output_schema -->
Return a JSON object with keys:
- "attack_map": list of live endpoint entries. Each entry is an object with
  fields: method (required), path (required), code_file, code_function,
  auth_required (bool), notes. code_file/code_function MUST cite a code entry
  point from the evidence.
- "reasons": list of strings explaining how each mapping was established (cite the
  code entry point + the observed live signal, e.g. status code).
- "proposed_http_specs": list of HTTP probe specs to dispatch. Each entry is an
  object with fields: method (required), path (required), headers, body,
  auth_profile, vuln_class, functional_area. Never inline credentials.
- "tool_calls": list of tool calls you want to make (empty list when done). Each
  entry must include kind, tool_name, args, reasoning (hypothesis, target_ref,
  expected_evidence, why_this_tool).

Example final response:

{"attack_map":[{"method":"GET","path":"/users/1","code_file":"app/users.py","code_function":"get_user","auth_required":false,"notes":"IDOR candidate"}],"reasons":["app/users.py:get_user handles /users/{id}; live GET /users/1 returned 200"],"proposed_http_specs":[{"method":"GET","path":"/users/1","vuln_class":"idor"}],"tool_calls":[]}
